{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c57d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0d50d-b8e8-7b33-a45d-f1920e40d897"},"sequence":281,"recorded_at":1780531400000557,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"16827b65-f82c-4989-a975-d74d7ed70709","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"16827b65-f82c-4989-a975-d74d7ed70709","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"16827b65-f82c-4989-a975-d74d7ed70709"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0d50e-d6c9-71e0-b2e5-ac4291cbb999"},"task_id":"01a0d50e-d6c9-71e0-b2e5-ac4291cbb999","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0d50e-d6c9-71e0-b2e5-ac4291cbb999","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/rev4-retry/results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260924-2zboyz — read-back manifest + validation report schemas — results (rev4)\n2|\n3|## Outcome\n4|\n5|Rework of CR rev3 answering the rev3 verdict's single finding\n6|(`report-sibling-provenance-unbound`, `repeat-of: none`;\n7|severity `bypass`). Package `internal/clonereadback` (new files\n8|only, no landed file touched): Clone Read-Back Evidence Manifest\n9|1.0.0 and Clone Validation Report 1.0.0 as closed schemas with\n10|JCS identities, pinned to `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`\n11|§13.14.2 (lines 10737-10777, prose 10580-10582, registry 170-171,\n12|ReadAuthority purpose 3796-3797). By construction (\"parse, don't\n13|validate\") the report entries accept ONLY sealed\n14|`ValidatedReadBack` siblings minted by the read-back validator:\n15|unexported fields, the two read-back entries as the only\n16|constructors, and the zero value refused at both report entries\n17|before any claim comparison. The generated\n18|`testdata/__pycache__` blob is REMOVED and a no-bytecode hygiene\n19|test pins its absence; the harness runs with `python3 -B`.\n20|Candidate is the uncommitted tree on story tip `5e40826` (=\n21|trunk `6d3bff9` + three signed story checkpoints). No registry\n22|edit (`task_delta`).\n23|\n24|## Verdict answers (finding → fix → regression → narrowing)\n25|\n26|| Finding | Fix | Named regression tests | Narrowings (killed alone) |\n27||---|---|---|---|\n28|| report-sibling-provenance-unbound | new sealed `ValidatedReadBack` (unexported fields; minted only by `Build/DecodeReadBackEvidenceManifest`); report entries take ONLY sealed siblings and refuse zero first via shared `checkSiblingsSealed` | `TestBuildReportRefusesUnsealedSiblings`, `TestDecodeReportRefusesUnsealedSiblings` (zero/zero, zero/sealed, sealed/zero × entry), `TestReportEntriesTakeOnlySealedSiblings` (AST: no struct/digest sibling param), `TestValidatedReadBackSealedConstruction` (AST+reflection: no exported fields/ctors + zero refused), `TestBuild/DecodeReportSiblingFromAnotherPlanIsBound` (cross-plan admission bound) | N-seal-build, N-seal-decode |\n29|| rev3 notes | `testdata/__pycache__/*.pyc` removed | `TestNoGeneratedBytecode` | — (hygiene, not a gate) |\n30|\n31|## AC coverage: 6 of 6 rows driven through production entries\n32|\n33|| AC row | Production call sites | Named tests |\n34||---|---|---|\n35|| Both schemas closed (reflection census, every member missing/extra/duplicated/miscased/wrong-type refused with literal code at every entry) | `DecodeReadBackEvidenceManifest`, `DecodeValidationReport` (+ `Build*` render exactness) | `TestMemberCensusExactSets`, `TestMemberCensusUnknownMissing`, `TestMemberCensusMiscased`, `TestMemberCensusWrongTypes`, `TestMemberCensusDuplicated`, `TestMemberCensusNoLiteralList`, `TestCensusShapeInventory` (16/5/23) |\n36|| Ids recomputed independently | `Build*` seal, `Decode*` verify | `TestReadBackIdentityIndependent`, `TestReportIdentityIndependent` (JCS recompute via `github.com/gowebpki/jcs` in-test) |\n37|| Staged/live modes cannot be relabeled | both read-back entries via `modeForAuthorityPurpose` + `checkModeAuthority` | `TestModeAuthorityGrid`, 4 relabel regressions, `TestModeRelabelRefused`, `TestModeBindsIdentity` |\n38|| Every applicable check must pass for valid=true (whole-domain oracle) | `BuildValidationReport`, `DecodeValidationReport` via shared `decideValid` | `TestValidWholeDomainOracle` (128 × 2 × 6 = 1536 combos through both entries) |\n39|| Every entry calls the owner validators (AST census) | all four entries → `sessadapter`/`clonebundle`/`environ`/`scalar`/`canonicaljson`; fidelity/plan row census empty; report siblings sealed-only | `TestOwnerRowCensusIsEmpty`, `TestOwnerReachability` (+ `checkSiblingsSealed` both-entries pin), `TestNoOwnerImports`, `TestExportedAPIInventory`, `TestNoForkedLiterals`, `TestNoForkedSelectors`, `TestErrorSeverityDecidedOnDecodedField`, `TestOwnerDelegation`, `TestReportEntriesTakeOnlySealedSiblings`, `TestValidatedReadBackSealedConstruction` |\n40|| Each gate has a narrowing killed alone | 43 narrowings + 1 neutral control + 9 structural plants | harness `testdata/mutant_harness.py` (53 rows), battery × 2 runs, one raw log per plant per run |\n41|\n42|Measured narrowing ratio: 18 of 18 counted gates carry ≥1\n43|narrowing killed alone (rev3's 17 + A20 sibling seal); 2 gates\n44|(owner-inner rules, extension value model) are justified\n45|delegated bounds excluded from the ratio, with wiring pinned\n46|behaviorally + structurally.\n47|\n48|## Gate verdicts (all green, exit codes observed)\n49|\n50|| Gate | Command | Exit | Evidence |\n51||---|---|---|---|\n52|| package suite | `go test -count=1 ./internal/clonereadback/` | 0 (56 PASS + 18 subtests, 0 FAIL) | `package-verbose.log` |\n53|| coverage | `go test -count=1 -cover ./internal/clonereadback/` | 0, 95.6% | `cover.log` |\n54|| importer set | owner suites `environ scalar canonicaljson clonebundle sessadapter` | 0 (all five `ok`) | `importer.log` |\n55|| vet | `go vet ./...` | 0 | `vet.log` |\n56|| windows vet | `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./...` | 0 | `vet-windows.log` |\n57|| gofmt | `gofmt -l internal/` | 0, clean | `gofmt.log` |\n58|| determinism | `go test -count=3 ./internal/clonereadback/` | 0 | `determinism.log` |\n59|| mutant battery run1 | `mutant_harness.py run run1` (53 rows) | 0, failures=0 | `run1/*.log` |\n60|| mutant battery run2 | `mutant_harness.py run run2` (53 rows) | 0, failures=0 | `run2/*.log` |\n61|| full suite shard1 (47 pkgs excl. traceability) | `go test -count=1 <47 pkgs>` | 1 (45 ok; `resumesmoke` + `tmuxserver` hit the 10m `go test` timeout under contention, zero import edge to this leaf) | `full-shard1.log` |\n62|| contention reruns | each package alone | 0 (`resumesmoke` 164.8s, `tmuxserver` 386.0s) | `rerun-resumesmoke.log`, `rerun-tmuxserver.log` |\n63|| full suite shard2 (traceability) | `go test -count=1` on both pkgs | 0 (2 ok, tracecheck 381.5s) | `full-shard2.log` |\n64|\n65|Full-suite total: 49 packages, all green (45 in-shard +\n66|2 contention-timeout packages green on alone rerun +\n67|2 traceability). The two timeouts are `panic: test timed out\n68|after 10m0s` under 47-way contention with no dependency path to\n69|`internal/clonereadback` (`go list -deps` shows zero edge),\n70|the same contention shape as the rev1 tracecheck episode; both\n71|pass alone with no code change.\n72|\n73|## Mutant summary (narrowing vs arm-delete per row)\n74|\n75|All 43 N-rows are narrowings (single-site; the gate stays\n76|present and admits exactly one forbidden member past the\n77|weakened site); there are no arm-deletes. Conjunct-drop rows\n78|(N-valid-drop-*, N-mode-auth-*, N-report-refs-*, N-seal-*)\n79|drop one conjunct at one call site; the N-seal kill is the\n80|fall-through to the downstream distinctness/slot refusal with a\n81|changed literal (the documented N-closed precedent: proves the\n82|seal gate's presence, first position, and literal). Killers ran\n83|ALONE (harness `-run`).\n84|\n85|| Mutant | Admits exactly | Killer (alone) | R1 | R2 |\n86||---|---|---|---|---|\n87|| N-mode-archived | `archived` mode | `TestModeVocabularyOracle` | K | K |\n88|| N-kind-native | `native